Description: adapt entry_ref/node_ref field access to the V\OS accessors
 V\OS encapsulates entry_ref and node_ref: the legacy public fields
 device/directory/node became accessor methods (device(), directory(),
 node()) with set_to() to bind values, so poking fields - and taking their
 addresses for BMessage::FindInt32/FindInt64 - no longer compiles. Read the
 message values into locals and bind them with set_to(); message keys and
 semantics are unchanged. The ref name member stays public, so name
 handling is untouched.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <packages@vitruvianos.org>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor, V\OS packaging
--- a/FSUtils.cpp
+++ b/FSUtils.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 	off_t src_bytes;
 
 	dest->GetRef(&ref);
-	BVolume dvolume(ref.device);
+	BVolume dvolume(ref.device());
 	src->GetSize(&src_bytes);
 
 	if (src_bytes > dvolume.FreeBytes())
